+# ExternalMeetingConnector interoperability research
+
+**Freshness:** 2026-08-08
+
+**Issue:** `1ba32c21-490d-4308-ba81-d6874b534ec4`
+
+**Scope:** decision/contract research only; no provider adoption or implementation.
+
+## Decision
+
+Use one provider-neutral `ExternalMeetingConnector` boundary for capture that occurs outside a Product-Suite-hosted room. Develop the existing browser-local path as the MVP, integrate Recall.ai only as an explicit fallback, and defer Zoom RTMS implementation while reserving a capability-compatible adapter slot. A one-shot artifact import is a connector mode, not a fourth authority.
+
+| Path | Choice | Bounded rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Browser-local capture | **DEVELOP** | It already exists in `useAudioRecorder` and `App.jsx`; place it behind the contract. Crash/network-safe slicing remains owned by sibling issue `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a`. |
+| Recall.ai | **INTEGRATE as fallback** | Use only when local capabilities fail or the user explicitly chooses a bot/desktop route. Product-Suite still owns meeting, transcript, ACL, retention, and run records. |
+| Zoom RTMS | **DEFER implementation** | RTMS is active and GA, but requires credits, fixed app scopes, participant disclosures, and product-specific operational validation. Preserve the contract seam and pilot only after the exit criteria below. |
+| Existing audio/transcript artifact | **IMPORT mode** | Accept a bounded, provenance-labelled artifact without pretending it was a live capture session. |
+
+## Boundary and authority
+
+`ExternalMeetingConnector` negotiates capture capabilities, starts/stops external capture, imports artifacts, reports status, and requests provider deletion. It emits canonical Product-Suite events and artifact references.
+
+It is intentionally distinct from:
+
+- `RoomProvider`: creates Product-Suite-hosted rooms, mints participant tokens, exports room audio, and reports export completion. The existing room-provider research already defines those four operations (`docs/research/2026-07-25-meeting-experience-and-livekit.md:284`).
+- `RealtimeAgentAdapter`: owns live agent media/turn/tool behavior, not meeting capture or transcript storage.
+
+Providers never own the canonical meeting, transcript, ACL, provenance, retention policy, or agent/run/proposal record. Provider payloads are inputs; the Product-Suite meeting service validates and projects them into canonical records.
+
+## Proposed minimum contract
+
+```text
+negotiate(request, policy) -> CapabilityDecision
+prepare(startRequest) -> PreparedCapture
+start(preparedId, idempotencyKey) -> ConnectorSession
+stop(connectorSessionId, idempotencyKey) -> StopResult
+importArtifact(importRequest, idempotencyKey) -> ArtifactReceipt
+status(connectorSessionId) -> ConnectorStatus
+delete(connectorSessionId, idempotencyKey) -> DeletionReceipt
+```
+
+`CapabilityDecision` reports source mode (`local_live`, `provider_bot`, `provider_rtms`, `artifact_import`), media available, transcript latency, consent mechanism, visible-indicator support, allowed region, provider retention, deletion support, availability, and estimated/reserved budget. Unsupported or policy-incompatible capabilities fail closed.
+
+Every canonical event includes `event_id`, `tenant_id`, `meeting_id`, `connector_session_id`, connector/version, provider event id when present, kind, occurred/received timestamps, semantic idempotency key, payload hash, artifact reference, completeness/gap state, and provenance. A verified server context—not provider metadata—derives tenant and actor identity.
+
+## Safety and lifecycle requirements
+
+- **Consent and recording indication:** start requires an authorized actor, an immutable consent-evidence reference, and a visible Product-Suite recording indicator. Revocation or indicator loss stops capture. Never silently switch to a more visible bot, a broader source, or a higher-cost path. Recall's desktop SDK explicitly leaves recording indication to the integrating app, so the wrapper indicator is mandatory. Zoom RTMS exposes participant disclosure/app-activity UX and app scopes to participants. [Recall desktop SDK](https://www.recall.ai/product/desktop-recording-sdk), [Zoom participant UX](https://godevelopers.zoom.us/docs/rtms/meetings/ux-participant), [W3C Screen Capture privacy indicators](https://www.w3.org/TR/screen-capture/)
+- **ACL and provenance:** meeting capture requires canonical meeting-write/capture permission plus organization policy. Read/delete follow canonical ACLs. Provider IDs and meeting URLs are untrusted provenance, never authorization selectors.
+- **Retention, deletion, regions:** Product-Suite applies its own raw-media/transcript/derived-data policy and records a deletion tombstone plus provider confirmation. Exact region is a negotiated allow-list; deny if a tenant-required region is unavailable. Recall defaults vary by account creation date, permanent deletion has caveats for custom metadata, and zero retention requires `retention:null`; therefore defaults must never be trusted. [Recall storage and playback](https://docs.recall.ai/docs/storage-and-playback)
+- **Retries and idempotency:** acknowledge verified provider webhooks quickly, process asynchronously, honor `Retry-After`, deduplicate provider events, and reject same-key/different-payload conflicts. Recall documents retry behavior, 409 backoff, 429 `Retry-After`, and 507 pool exhaustion. [Recall webhook lifecycle](https://docs.recall.ai/v1.10/docs/bot-status-change-events), [Recall errors](https://docs.recall.ai/reference/errors)
+- **Outages and gaps:** surface `degraded`, `interrupted`, `incomplete`, and `deletion_pending`; never invent missing media/transcript. Fallback that changes consent, participant visibility, region, or price requires fresh user confirmation. Local durable queue/retry behavior is delegated to the sibling issue.
+- **Cost budgets:** reserve against per-meeting duration and org monthly recording/storage budgets before provider start; warn near thresholds and deny or stop at a hard cap. Pricing stays configurable and date-stamped, never compiled into the contract. Zoom says RTMS consumes Developer Pack credits; Recall bills storage after its included window. [Zoom RTMS overview](https://developers.zoom.us/docs/rtms/), [Recall storage and playback](https://docs.recall.ai/docs/storage-and-playback)
+
+## Current platform evidence
+
+- Browser screen capture requires a secure context, transient user activation, a fresh user choice, and has browser-varying audio support. [MDN `getDisplayMedia`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaDevices/getDisplayMedia)
+- `MediaRecorder` timeslices are not exact and may produce delayed/larger chunks, so chunk count is not elapsed time and the connector must preserve observed timestamps/gaps. [MDN `dataavailable`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaRecorder/dataavailable_event)
+- Recall supports real-time transcript/participant webhooks and WebSocket media; its guidance recommends fast webhook acknowledgement and idempotent asynchronous work. [Recall meeting-bot guide](https://www.recall.ai/blog/how-to-build-a-meeting-bot)
+- Zoom RTMS is GA (June 25, 2025), has ongoing 2026 SDK/releases, and provides audio/video/transcript streams without a bot. It requires a General app, Developer Pack credits, RTMS lifecycle events, and fixed granular scopes. [RTMS changelog](https://developers.zoom.us/changelog/rtms), [RTMS features](https://developers.zoom.us/docs/rtms/meetings/add-features/)
+
+## Zoom RTMS defer exit criteria
+
+Implement only after all are true: current credit price/budget is approved; OAuth/scopes/admin approval and participant disclosure are reviewed; tenant-region and deletion expectations are documented; concurrency/failover behavior is load-tested; a small consented pilot proves the selected runtime can maintain RTMS connections; and expected volume justifies another operational adapter. The capability response remains `supported: false, reason: deferred_policy` until then.
+
+## Threat-model and test implications
+
+OWASP coverage required in implementation: server-derived ACLs (A01), verified webhook/auth boundaries (A07), schema and payload-size validation (A03/A04), encrypted transport/storage and secret rotation (A02), safe defaults/region policy (A05), dependency scanning (A06), signed provenance/audit events (A08/A09), and bounded concurrency/timeouts/circuit breakers (A10).
+
+Contract tests must cover unauthorized start/delete, missing or revoked consent, indicator failure, unsupported region, over-budget denial, duplicate/out-of-order webhook, same idempotency key with a different payload, partial media gap, retry exhaustion, deletion pending/confirmed, artifact import provenance, and an attempted provider payload that selects another tenant.
+
+## Research limitations
+
+Current provider pricing, exact region inventory, tenant-specific Zoom entitlements, and production concurrency were not verified from an account. They are runtime/onboarding inputs, not assumptions. The broad repository `bun test` baseline was incomplete/failing because it collected Vitest/Playwright suites under the root Bun harness and lacked browser/Supabase environment; no failure was attributed to this documentation-only branch.
