+# ExternalMeetingConnector interoperability plan
+
+**Date:** 2026-08-08
+
+**Issue:** `1ba32c21-490d-4308-ba81-d6874b534ec4`
+
+**Status:** Draft for plan review; no implementation authorized.
+
+## Purpose
+
+Define one provider-neutral boundary for browser-local meeting capture, a Recall.ai fallback, deferred Zoom RTMS, and artifact import without granting any provider meeting, transcript, ACL, retention, or run authority.
+
+## Success criteria
+
+- A small contract distinguishes external capture from `RoomProvider` and `RealtimeAgentAdapter`.
+- Every start is capability-, policy-, consent-, region-, ACL-, and budget-checked.
+- Canonical events are provenance-rich and idempotent; partial/outage states remain explicit.
+- Local is the bounded MVP, Recall is an explicit fallback, Zoom RTMS remains deferred behind objective exit criteria.
+- Provider deletion and Product-Suite retention are independently observable.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+Room hosting, participant-token minting, realtime agent turns/tools, provider-owned transcripts/runs, automatic fallback without renewed disclosure, Zoom RTMS implementation, browser extension/desktop system-audio implementation, and local crash/network durability owned by sibling issue `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a`.
+
+## Selected approach
+
+Add a versioned contract with seven operations: `negotiate`, `prepare`, `start`, `stop`, `importArtifact`, `status`, and `delete`. The meeting service remains the orchestration and authority layer. Adapters translate provider/local events to canonical connector envelopes; downstream transcription and agent execution consume canonical artifacts only.
+
+The selection order is policy, not hidden failover: local when requested capabilities and consent UX are available; Recall only after explicit fallback choice and cost/region preflight; import for an existing artifact; Zoom returns a deferred capability until its exit criteria pass.
+
+## Constraints and invariants
+
+- Server context derives tenant/actor; provider fields cannot select authorization scope.
+- `start` requires consent evidence and an active visible indicator; revocation stops capture.
+- Same idempotency key plus different semantics is a conflict, never a second session.
+- Webhooks are acknowledged quickly and handled asynchronously with dedupe/backoff.
+- Exact region and hard budget are negotiated inputs; unsupported means deny.
+- Product-Suite retention/deletion policy applies even when provider deletion is pending.
+- Gaps, interruptions, and incomplete deletion are durable states, not success.
+
+## Edge cases
+
+Permission denied after preflight; local source ends mid-meeting; indicator process crashes; bot pool exhaustion; duplicate/out-of-order webhook; provider reconnect changes stream identity; webhook outage exceeds provider retry window; transcript arrives before audio metadata; deletion confirmation never arrives; region changes between prepare/start; monthly budget is consumed concurrently; imported artifact hash collides with different provenance.
+
+## Ambiguity policy
+
+Choose the privacy-preserving, lower-cost, non-recording outcome. Do not broaden media, switch provider, or extend retention without explicit policy and user confirmation. Unknown provider state maps to `degraded` or `incomplete`, never `complete`.
+
+## Technical research
+
+The evidence, live-source freshness, contract sketch, threat model, and vendor choices are in [`docs/research/externalmeetingconnector-interoperability.md`](../../research/externalmeetingconnector-interoperability.md). Existing code anchors are `packages/contracts/src/meeting.js`, `apps/meeting-web/src/hooks/useAudioRecorder.js`, `apps/meeting-web/src/App.jsx`, and `apps/meeting-api/backend/server.py`.
+
+## Plan-review gates
+
+1. Confirm local-first + explicit Recall fallback is the MVP product choice.
+2. Confirm the meeting service, not a new control plane, owns connector sessions and canonical events.
+3. Confirm Zoom RTMS stays contract-only/deferred until every exit criterion passes.
+4. Confirm sibling issue `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a` owns local durability so implementation tasks do not overlap.
