+# ExternalMeetingConnector implementation tasks
+
+**Status:** Proposed only; execute under `/dev` after plan approval.
+
+## Task 1 — Versioned shared contract
+
+**Owns:** `packages/contracts/contracts/meeting-external-connector.json`, `packages/contracts/src/meeting.js`, `packages/contracts/src/index.d.ts`, focused contract tests.
+
+RED: tests reject missing consent/tenant/provenance, invalid capability combinations, and same idempotency key with changed semantics.
+GREEN: add the minimum operations, capability decision, canonical event, artifact receipt, and lifecycle states.
+REFACTOR: keep provider names out of canonical types except a provenance identifier.
+
+## Task 2 — Product-owned policy/orchestration core
+
+**Owns:** a focused connector module under `apps/meeting-api/backend/` and its unit tests; no provider network code.
+
+RED: unauthorized start/delete, unsupported region, expired consent, over-budget reservation, and provider-supplied tenant selection fail closed.
+GREEN: implement negotiation, ACL/policy checks, budget reservation, state transitions, dedupe, and canonical event persistence through existing meeting authority.
+REFACTOR: separate pure policy decisions from I/O.
+
+## Task 3 — Browser-local adapter seam
+
+**Owns:** adapter wiring around `apps/meeting-web/src/hooks/useAudioRecorder.js` and `apps/meeting-web/src/App.jsx`; consumes sibling durability protocol rather than reimplementing it.
+
+RED: user gesture/permission denial, visible-indicator loss, revocation, source-ended, and gap reporting tests.
+GREEN: expose local capabilities and translate existing capture lifecycle to connector commands/events.
+REFACTOR: keep browser APIs outside the shared contract.
+
+## Task 4 — Recall fallback adapter
+
+**Owns:** Recall-specific adapter, webhook verifier/translator, fixtures, and conformance tests.
+
+RED: invalid signature, duplicate/out-of-order webhook, 409/429/507 retry instructions, deletion pending, unsupported region, and fallback without renewed confirmation.
+GREEN: implement prepare/start/stop/status/delete and canonical translation behind the shared boundary.
+REFACTOR: isolate Recall payloads and configurable pricing/retention metadata.
+
+## Task 5 — Consent, indicator, capability and budget UX
+
+**Owns:** meeting-web connector chooser/status UI and focused accessibility tests.
+
+RED: no start without disclosure/consent; provider/price/region changes require reconfirmation; indicator and degraded/incomplete states remain visible and screen-reader announced.
+GREEN: implement local-first selection, explicit Recall fallback, hard-budget denial, stop/delete controls, and provenance/status display.
+REFACTOR: share presentation over canonical capability/status data.
+
+## Task 6 — Conformance and operational evidence
+
+**Owns:** adapter conformance suite, runbook/reference docs, and metrics with no raw media/transcript payloads.
+
+RED: every adapter must pass lifecycle, idempotency, outage, deletion, ACL, provenance, region, consent, and budget scenarios.
+GREEN: add fixtures for local, Recall, import, and Zoom-deferred capability; document alarms and deletion reconciliation.
+REFACTOR: ensure telemetry contains identifiers/hashes/states only.
+
+## Explicit deferral
+
+Do not implement Zoom RTMS in these tasks. After the research exit criteria pass, file/claim a separate issue with its own adapter and operational pilot. Do not absorb sibling issue `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a` (local crash/network-safe persistence and retry).
